When splitting massive context components in Next.js, isolate the state management and transition logic into a dedicated hook (e.g., `hooks/usePlaylistPlaybackState.ts`). Move the complex implementation details there, but retain the Context definition, the Context Provider wrapper, and the exported types inside the original context file. In the original file, re-export the hook and types to maintain a stable external API while drastically improving file readability and separating concerns.
